    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0597" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2539½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5969</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-13">November 13,
                        1941</date>.<lb/>[Received March 31, 1942.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to submit herewith
                    Strictly Confidential Fortnightly Background Report No. 3 from the Commercial
                    Attaché for the period from October 27th to November 8th. I entirely concur in
                    Mr. Williams’ appraisal of the situation in Japan and in this connection
                    reference is respectfully made to my strictly confidential telegram No. 1736,
                    November 3, 3 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d437-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph C. Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d437-a1.xml" xpointer="d437-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
